== Nested timelines ==
An item can hold its own timeline, indented under it, through the <code>sub</code> parameter.

{{User:Fanaro009/Timeline sandbox
|{{User:Fanaro009/Timeline sandbox/item |date=1960s–1990s |title=Hand-written programs |text=Engines encode Go knowledge by hand. |sub=
{{User:Fanaro009/Timeline sandbox/item |date=1968 |title=First Go program |text=Albert Zobrist writes a program able to play a full game.}}
{{User:Fanaro009/Timeline sandbox/item |date=1990s |title=Neural networks meet Go |text=Learning-based programs appear. |sub=
{{User:Fanaro009/Timeline sandbox/item |date=1994 |title=NeuroGo}}
{{User:Fanaro009/Timeline sandbox/item |date=1996 |title=Golem}}
}}
}}
{{User:Fanaro009/Timeline sandbox/item |date=2016 |title=AlphaGo defeats Lee Sedol |text=AlphaGo wins four games to one in Seoul.}}
}}

== Compact variant ==
A dense list with a solid bar, through <code>compact=yes</code>. A date can have no events.

{{User:Fanaro009/Timeline sandbox |compact=yes
|{{User:Fanaro009/Timeline sandbox/item |date=1846 |title=The Ear-Reddening Game}}
{{User:Fanaro009/Timeline sandbox/item |date=1847}}
{{User:Fanaro009/Timeline sandbox/item |date=1924 |title=Nihon Ki-in founded}}
{{User:Fanaro009/Timeline sandbox/item |date=2006 |events=
{{User:Fanaro009/Timeline sandbox/event |title=Crazy Stone}}
{{User:Fanaro009/Timeline sandbox/event |title=UCT}}
}}
{{User:Fanaro009/Timeline sandbox/item |date=2016 |title=AlphaGo defeats Lee Sedol}}
}}

